# Pewhipee support

Pewhipee is a memory-game app that builds puzzles from photos on this iPhone. There is no account and no server.

**Need help?** Email [prater10@icloud.com](mailto:prater10@icloud.com)  
Please include your iPhone model and iOS version.

## Photos access

Today and Games need access to Photos so Pewhipee can pick a picture.

1. Open **Settings → Pewhipee → Photos**.
2. Choose **Limited Access** or **Full Access**.
3. If you chose Limited Access, tap **Edit Selected Photos** and pick the albums that are fair game.

Originals in Photos are never changed. Deleting Pewhipee data only removes copies inside the app.

## Microphone

Talking Memories can record a short story. That is optional.

**Settings → Pewhipee → Microphone**

Recordings stay on this phone.

## Notifications

Daily reminders are optional and scheduled on this device.

Turn them on in **Pewhipee → Book → Settings**.

## A game won’t open

- Allow Photos access, or add a few pictures in Memories.
- Map Memory only works with photos that already have a location.
- Gone and Rewind unlock after a few mixes in the Book.
- If a picture can’t make a fair puzzle, choose **Try another picture**.

## Sharing a challenge

Send challenge uses the system share sheet (Messages, Mail, AirDrop). The puzzle travels inside the picture. Save the original file, not a screenshot — a screenshot loses the puzzle.

The other person opens Pewhipee, picks the picture they received, and plays your round.

## Pass and play

Two players, one phone. It is not an online match. Scores stay on that device.

## Delete my data

In the app: **Book → Settings → Delete all Pewhipee data**.

That removes Pewhipee’s copies, stories, and play history. Your originals in Photos are untouched. Uninstalling the app also removes everything Pewhipee stored on the phone.

